                        "form": "dickered"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "218c15ba-9219-3801-9d35-50df9a6ffc83",
                        "entry_id": "dce564d5-673d-3d4e-9e99-424c0faab75d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To bargain, haggle or negotiate over a sale."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "intransitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "20764277-3349-4fa4-b24e-1dbddd18e05b",
                                "sense_id": "218c15ba-9219-3801-9d35-50df9a6ffc83",
                                "text": "At Bouira the detachment detrained, and the balance of the journey was made in the saddle. As Tarzan was dickering at Bouira for a mount he caught a brief glimpse of a man in European clothes eying him from the doorway of a native coffeehouse, […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "55d9be1c-220d-46a9-a0fa-25ece75ef6b8",
                                "sense_id": "218c15ba-9219-3801-9d35-50df9a6ffc83",
                                "text": "In the brilliant sparkle of the morning when everything that was not superlatively blue was superlatively green, I dickered with a man who was taking a party up the inlet that he should drop me off at the village I was headed for."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3a4d0b6c-07b9-368e-961d-0f311f0fc989",
                        "entry_id": "dce564d5-673d-3d4e-9e99-424c0faab75d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To barter."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "intransitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d8337551-4eb4-4238-a669-11ef6e004d95",
                                "sense_id": "3a4d0b6c-07b9-368e-961d-0f311f0fc989",
                                "text": "Then, the white men who penetrated to those semi-wilds were always ready to \"dicker\" and to \"swap,\" and to \"trade\" rifles, and watches, and whatever else they might happen to possess, almost to their wives and children."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ef729ac6-3cbe-3dd6-b749-c086c54819ff",
                        "entry_id": "dce564d5-673d-3d4e-9e99-424c0faab75d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To fiddle."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "intransitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0608102e-1cd5-4798-92f7-b41bfbfe1918",
                                "sense_id": "ef729ac6-3cbe-3dd6-b749-c086c54819ff",
                                "text": "They sat in a booth near the door and drank the first cold ones of the evening while watching three impassioned pinballers dickering with flashing, promising, tilting machines."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
